    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "25bc9092-b020-3bde-86f3-5c04d656e7f1",
                "word": "statuary",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6ae6a7e7-6771-4060-a24a-24f67d41de84",
                        "entry_id": "25bc9092-b020-3bde-86f3-5c04d656e7f1",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more statuary"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d775b9a7-7433-436a-9530-c97b297e95d5",
                        "entry_id": "25bc9092-b020-3bde-86f3-5c04d656e7f1",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most statuary"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17749148-7551-306b-87c5-157205117a77",
                        "entry_id": "25bc9092-b020-3bde-86f3-5c04d656e7f1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, relating to, or characteristic of statues."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "941cd59c-5c78-4156-a852-9cfc7867c25d",
                                "sense_id": "17749148-7551-306b-87c5-157205117a77",
                                "text": "He [Francis Bacon] lyeth interred in the Church of St. Michael at St. Albans in Hartfordſhire, and hath there a fair ſtatuary monument erected for him of white Marble at the coſt of Sir Thomas Meautis, his ancient ſervant, who was not neerer to him living then dead: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c6d7a40-f6cc-4b6d-862e-8aa77b4a0d6b",
                                "sense_id": "17749148-7551-306b-87c5-157205117a77",
                                "text": "There is the lady’s own book, complete without a teacher—showing how the waist should be boddiced; the parasol handled; the statuary attitudes; the Parisian curtsy; the prettiest toss of the head, and swing of the train."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb9cfff5-166e-424e-a34e-76894b94bf26",
                                "sense_id": "17749148-7551-306b-87c5-157205117a77",
                                "text": "Characteristically, the photo series ends with the trainer having successfully contorted the boy’s body into a classical, statuary pose, even as the boy forces a pained smile for the camera."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "a8e499af-ea42-30e9-90bb-751273b6c71e",
                "word": "statuary",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ab44689-991b-3676-a368-279baece3e3c",
                        "entry_id": "a8e499af-ea42-30e9-90bb-751273b6c71e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The craft of making statues."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5226cd8e-88b1-39ac-8db9-a237dc7022d0",
                        "entry_id": "a8e499af-ea42-30e9-90bb-751273b6c71e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Statues considered collectively."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "408972ed-64de-414d-95fe-557f946dd2a0",
                                "sense_id": "5226cd8e-88b1-39ac-8db9-a237dc7022d0",
                                "text": "Simply on aesthetic grounds I can almost applaud the Victorians’ fig obsessed Bowdlerisation of Greek and Roman statuary."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9ae7b70-bdd1-4aba-a15c-46754e1a78ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8e499af-ea42-30e9-90bb-751273b6c71e",
                        "source_sense_description": "craft of making statues",
                        "target_lang_word": "statuaire",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "statuaire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f96445f-e794-37ef-a671-5a9096e3bb1c",
                                        "entry_id": "b07de0ee-9113-3df8-9d22-ad83c578fbb0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui concerne les statues."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sculpture"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c83daf3-a02c-43b2-a0cf-3c34d7e68d10",
                                                "sense_id": "2f96445f-e794-37ef-a671-5a9096e3bb1c",
                                                "text": "Art statuaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2592bad7-fc11-49c7-803a-56f94662b5cd",
                                                "sense_id": "2f96445f-e794-37ef-a671-5a9096e3bb1c",
                                                "text": "Marbre statuaire, Marbre propre à faire des statues, qui est blanc et sans aucune tache ni veine, à la différence de celui qu’on emploie aux ouvrages d’architecture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20c07023-d0f9-3566-8e6a-42df211f4f3e",
                                        "entry_id": "b07de0ee-9113-3df8-9d22-ad83c578fbb0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui rappelle une statue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbadb0f8-0e47-4aa3-b22b-4a1333f025f2",
                                                "sense_id": "20c07023-d0f9-3566-8e6a-42df211f4f3e",
                                                "text": "Assise sur la natte, elle n'avait pas de mur derrière elle, pourtant elle se tenait droite, sans effort apparent, et j'étais troublé par la courbe de son cou, d'une pureté statuaire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "statuaire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97c74cbb-6e2e-3c11-bf0b-40565677bb82",
                                        "entry_id": "c2be24fc-e05f-3bbd-9822-1d5d07cfcd0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sculpteur qui fait des statues."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sculpture"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9d56912-7014-4c5d-84a5-45f9ad2a1214",
                                                "sense_id": "97c74cbb-6e2e-3c11-bf0b-40565677bb82",
                                                "text": "Il savait parfaitement que Craquot, statuaire de grand talent mais de pauvres relations, incapable de décrocher une commande, mijotait dans la gêne atroce."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "statuaire",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46bdc4ab-dd77-3b04-9604-48aad33239bc",
                                        "entry_id": "e5a9cce7-5ee2-3be5-9e27-201c2061a7a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Art de faire des statues."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70f68ad8-07a1-488b-8539-9dd84c442969",
                                                "sense_id": "46bdc4ab-dd77-3b04-9604-48aad33239bc",
                                                "text": "Ils ont seulement suivi l’exemple des Romains, qui dépouillèrent la Grèce des chefs-d’œuvre de la peinture et de la statuaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df2f682f-1a4a-417c-bc58-d8b8d5e42365",
                                                "sense_id": "46bdc4ab-dd77-3b04-9604-48aad33239bc",
                                                "text": "Terpsichore est une Muse du midi ; je présume qu’elle était très-brune, et qu’elle a souvent agité ses pieds dans les blés dorés ; ses mouvements, pleins d’une cadence précise, sont autant de divins motifs pour la statuaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2154d18-8d7f-496a-a76b-56d5637b9c9e",
                                                "sense_id": "46bdc4ab-dd77-3b04-9604-48aad33239bc",
                                                "text": "La position de la tête est originale puisqu'elle est inclinée vers l'épaule droite, cette amorce de mouvement étant unique dans la statuaire mégalithique corse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c57797b2-335a-4cdc-926c-a6b2db7f5513",
                                                "sense_id": "46bdc4ab-dd77-3b04-9604-48aad33239bc",
                                                "text": "L'architecture et la statuaire eurent à regretter un grand nombre de chefs-d'œuvre, victimes de ce vandalisme chrétien qui précéda celui des Barbares. Le célèbre saint Martin de Tours ne laissa pas un temple, pas une pierre fitte, pas un chêne, consacré par le druidisme, debout dans son diocèse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e67223e-5b5f-4b82-89ad-f312217d887c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8e499af-ea42-30e9-90bb-751273b6c71e",
